{"name":"Swim","hex":"#6bb8b5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Swim","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Swim"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swimming","blocks":[{"text":"Swimming is the self-propulsion of a person through water, usually for recreation, sport, exercise, or survival. Swimmers achieve locomotion by coordinating limb and body movements to achieve a level of buoyancy and hydrodynamic thrust that results in directional motion. For example, they float to a greater or lesser extent, and move in a given direction by coordinating their forward thrusting actions, especially of their head and torso, with other actions such as stroking with their arms and kicking with their legs. Swimming is a whole body exercise that requires endurance, skill and efficient techniques to maximize speed and minimize energy consumption."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/40._Schwimmzonen-_und_Mastersmeeting_Enns_2017_100m_Brust_Herren_USC_Traun-9897.jpg/330px-40._Schwimmzonen-_und_Mastersmeeting_Enns_2017_100m_Brust_Herren_USC_Traun-9897.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swimming"},{"title":"Competitive swimming","blocks":[{"text":"Swimming is an individual or team racing sport that requires the use of one's entire body to move through water. The sport takes place in pools or open water. Competitive swimming is one of the most popular Olympic sports, with varied distance events in butterfly, backstroke, breaststroke, freestyle, and individual medley. In addition to these individual events, four swimmers can take part in either a freestyle or medley relay. A medley relay consists of four swimmers who will each swim a different stroke, ordered as backstroke, breaststroke, butterfly and freestyle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Depart4x100.jpg/330px-Depart4x100.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Competitive_swimming"},{"title":"Swim (BTS song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Swim\" is a song by South Korean boy band BTS. It was released on March 20, 2026, as the lead single of the group's sixth Korean-language studio album Arirang. It is produced by Tyler Spry and Leclair, and written by James Essien, Sean Foreman, Tyler Spry, Jamison Baken, Ryan Tedder, RM, Kirsten Allyssa Spencer, Derrick Milano, and Pdogg."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/BTS_-_Keep_Swimming_%28cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swim_(BTS_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swimmers perform squats prior to entering the pool in a U.S. military base, 2011.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParticipants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Fos